# BlackFlagCoop — Cursor handoff & safety

## Before starting any milestone

1. Read `README.md` and the latest `docs/CHATGPT_HANDOFF.md`.
2. Read `reports/CHATGPT_HANDOFF.json` for machine-readable status.
3. Inspect Git status and the latest commit (`git status`, `git log -5 --oneline`).
4. Read relevant files under `docs/` and `reports/` for the topic before repeating investigations.
5. Confirm you are on **PC1** only: `C:\Users\Frees\OneDrive\Documents\BlackFlagCoop`.

## Project constants

- Game target: **Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced 1.0.6** (`ACBlackFlag.exe`).
- Preferred generator: **Visual Studio 18 2026**, **-A x64**.
- Working in-game ASI: **v0.5.1** — do not deploy or replace without explicit user approval.
- Repository: `https://github.com/zzyrrup/BlackFlagCoop`.

## Research vs runtime

- Keep **offline executable research** (PE/string/callgraph tools under `tools/offline/`) separate from **live runtime** work.
- Offline analysis: no game launch, no inject/hooks, no live memory R/W, no exe/asset/save mods.
- Never claim unverified game functionality. Label **confirmed** vs **hypothesis** explicitly.

## Safety (hard rules)

- Work on **PC1 only**. Do not modify PC2.
- Do not modify either game installation.
- Do not deploy or replace the working ASI v0.5.1 unless the user explicitly approves.
- Do not change the game executable or Ubisoft assets.
- Preserve existing research and `backups/` (local; not committed).
- Never commit credentials, tokens, private keys, game binaries, ASI binaries, or proprietary game assets.
- Never force-push. Never overwrite remote history.
- Never automatically push unreviewed or untested changes.
- Never spawn characters or attempt co-op actor injection unless the user explicitly authorizes that milestone.

## Completion requirements

Before declaring a milestone complete:

1. Run relevant tests/builds and record results.
2. Record exact changed files, test results, hashes (EXE/ASI when touched), and limitations.
3. Update `docs/CHATGPT_HANDOFF.md` and `reports/CHATGPT_HANDOFF.json`.
4. Commit only when the user asks; push only when the user asks and safety review passes.
5. Do not deploy without explicit user approval.

## Handoff to ChatGPT

After a pushed milestone, ChatGPT reviews GitHub diffs + handoff docs and returns next instructions. Cursor executes locally, evidences in docs/reports, then commits/pushes when requested.
